**/*/target/
**/*/result/

# target/
result
eval-store

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local TopoTestix run store
.topotestix/

# Thesis-eval reproduction: raw per-unit VM/nix console logs and in-progress
# staging dirs are large (~340 MB/campaign) and fully regenerable. The distilled
# analysis/verification/resolution artifacts and all *.json/*.csv evidence
# under experiments/thesis-evals-*/ are kept; only *.log files under raw/ are
# excluded (unit-level stdout/stderr.log and per-trial run-store logs alike).
#
# analyze.py does read those logs (test-suite counts, the etcd v1 startup error
# message), so each unit also carries a COMMITTED log-digest.json — a bounded
# projection of its logs (runner.write_log_digest) that collect.py falls back
# to when the *.log files are absent. That is what keeps analysis a function of
# what raw/ holds in git. Regenerate it with `--phase digest` after any run
# whose logs were produced outside run_unit.
experiments/thesis-evals-*/raw/**/*.log
experiments/thesis-evals-*/**/*.partial/

# Kafka campaign runs: per-run broker journals and VM console logs
# (~5 MB/run) are large and fully regenerable, so they stay outside git.
# kafka-rack-links analysis consumes the log_digest inside each run's
# committed kafka-rack-links-result.json, and a committed logs-manifest.sha256
# (campaign.py manifest) records a checksum for every excluded file.
# kafka-topology analysis reads only the committed JSON artifacts, so its run
# logs are debug-only. The small per-unit console captures under each
# campaign's logs/ directory are committed.
experiments/kafka-rack-links/*/runs/**/*.log
experiments/kafka-topology/**/runs/**/*.log
